    "formal": "x \\equiv a_i \\pmod{I_i}, \\quad i = 1, 2, 3",
    "plain": "The Chinese Remainder Theorem for coprime moduli is classical. The gallery entry `chinese-remainder-non-coprime-oq-02` generalizes to 2 non-coprime moduli. This problem extends to 3 moduli: the solvability condition is pairwise compatibility ($a_i \\equiv a_j \\pmod{I_i + I_j}$ for all pairs), and the solution space is unique mod the intersection $I_1 \\cap I_2 \\cap I_3$.",
